  "raw_text": "56\n\nDabi kaikaia\n \n(\ndict,dictu,db\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto taste\n \n/ probar\n\n(Note/Nota:\n \nPi kaikaia\n \nseems to be more commonly used /\n \nPi kaikaia\n \nparece ser más comúnmente usado)\n\nDadaukra\n \n(see/ver:\n \nDaukaia\n)\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \ndoer, maker, creator\n \n/ hacedor, fabricante, creador\n\nDahn/Dan\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nDanh\n\nDahra\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ntale, story, news, report, history, information, account\n \n/ cuento, historia, noticias, informe, información,\npasaje\n\n(Construct:\n \nDaihra\n \n–\n \nmy story...\n \n/ mi historia\n…\n;\n \nDamhra\n \n(a/t:\n \nDahmra\n \nin\n \ndict\n)\n \n–\n \nyour story...\n \n/ tu historia\n…\n)\n\nDahra aisaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto speak of, to relate, to bear witness, to announce, to tell history, to prophesy, to talk about\n \n/\nhablar, relatar, dar testimonio, anunciar, contar historia, profetizar\n\nDahra aisi ba\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \naccount, story\n \n/ relato, historia\n\nDahra aisanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nprophecy,\n \n…\n \n/ profecía\n, …\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nPrapit aisanka, Prapit dahra\naisanka\n \n–\n \nprophecy\n \n/ profecía)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-02/20\n):\n \nAni prapit dahra aisanka nani Baibil ra taki ba naiwa piua ra tnata aimakisa ki?\n \n–\n \nWhich Bible\n\nprophecies are being fulfilled in today’s time?\n \n/ ¿Qué profecías bíblicas se están cumpliendo en el tiempo de\nhoy?)\n\nSmaya dahra aisaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto predict\n \n/ predecir\n\nDahra kwahkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto report, to accuse, to gossip, to slander\n \n/ denunciar, acusar, chismear, calumniar\n\n(Lit:\n \nto bring/carry a report/story/accusation\n \n/ traer/llevar un informe/historia/acusación\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n-\n09/20\n):\n \nAman kaikpi turi kunin kum dahra kwahkbiara\n \n–\n \nLet’s be careful not to report a false story\n \n(false\n\ninformation)\n \n/\n \nTengamos cuidado de no informar una historia falsa (informaci\nó\nn falsa)\n)\n\nDahra kwakwahkra\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \naccuser\n \n/ acusador\n\n(Note/Nota:\n \nslanderer\n \n/ calumniador\n \n–\n \nNina aisasara\n-\ndb\n,\n \nDahra kwakwahkra\n-\ndb\n,\n \nNina sasauhkra\n-\ndict,lv\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\ndb\n-\nParam Marikan\n \n12:10\n):\n \nwan muihni nani dahra kwakwahkra\n \n–\n \naccuser of our\n \nbrothers\n \n/ acusador de\n\nnuestros hermanos\n)\n\nDahra sakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto denounce, to accuse, to report\n \n/ denunciar, acusar, notificar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb90\n):\n \nNaha waitnika\n \nra dîa tâwan dahra\n \nsakisma?\n \n–\n \n(For) what reason (do) you accuse this man?\n \n/ ¿Por qué razón\n\n(acusas) a este hombre?\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu\n-\n05/\n21\n):\n \nNisas ba smalkanka kuninkira nani ba dahra sakan\n \n–\n \nJesus denounced wrong teachings\n \n/ Jes\nú\ns\n\ndenunci\nó\n \nlas ense\nñ\nanzas falsas\n)\n\nDahra istikira sakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto draw conclusions\n \n/ sacar conclusiones\n\nWan dahra sakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto accuse oneself, to confess\n \n/ acusarse, confesarse\n\nDaikaia\n \n(v-trans; intrans:\n \nDaiwaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto pull out, to unearth, to pull off, to pluck, to take off, to eradicate\n \n/ sacar,\ndesenterrar, arrancar, despegar, erradicar\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nlfb18\n):\n \nSûskam nani ba daiks\n \n–\n \nTake your shoes off\n \n/ Quitate tus zapatos)\n\nIp daikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto pull out\n \n/ arrancar\n\nKwala daikaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nKuala daikaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto undress, to take clothes off\n \n/ desnudarse, quitarse la ropa\n\nDaiman\n \n(\ntc\n;\n \nDaimans\n-\ndictu\n,\ndict\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \ndiamond\n \n/ diamante\n\nDairiksan\n \n(a/t:\n \nDiriksan\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ndirections, address\n \n/ dirección\n\nDairit\n \n(\nmwb-03/20\n) (adv)\n \n–\n \ndirectly\n \n/ directamente\n\nDaiwaia\n \n(v-intrans; trans:\n \nDaikaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto be pulled out, to be unearthed, to be pulled off, to be plucked, to be eradicated\n \n/\nser sacado, ser desenterrado, ser arrancado, ser erradicado\n\nLal daiwra\n \n–\n \nbald head, bald\n \n/ cabeza calva, calvo,\n \npelón\n\nDaiwan\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nanimal, beast\n \n/ animal, bestia\n\n(Construct irreg:\n \nDaiwri\n \n–\n \nmy animal\n \n/ mi animal;\n \nDaiwram\n \n–\n \nyour animal\n \n/ tu animal;\n \nAi daiwra\n \n–\n \nhis/her/their animal\n \n/ su animal\n)\n\nDaiwan âiikra\n \n(a/t:\n \nDaiwan âikra\n \n(Aikra)\n) (n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nkiller of animals, hunter\n \n/ asesino de animales,\ncazador\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nAntin tatakra\n)\n\nDaiwan saura\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nwild beast\n \n/ bestia salvaje\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-12/19\n):\n \nDaiwan saura markka ba yawan briaia apia sa\n \n–\n \nWe must not have the mark of the wild beast\n \n/ No\ndebemos tener la marca de la bestia salvaje)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb12/19\n):\n \nDaiwan saura bara prapit kuninkira ba sauhki tikan kabia\n \n–\n \nThe wild beast and the false prophet will be\ndestroyed\n \n/ La bestia salvaje y el falso profeta serán destruidos)\n\nDaiwan tânka pliki kakaira\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nzoologist\n \n(\nmwb-01/20\n)\n, person who studies animals\n \n/ zoólogo (\nmwb-01/20\n),\npersona que estudia animales",
